// @check
// WHAT PRODUCED THE ABSENCE is the axis. Four conditions leave a diagnostic with no
// type to name, and this file MOVES that condition while holding the render POSITION
// fixed (a nested component of a composite, never the whole subject) and — for the
// first three — the message TEMPLATE fixed too (`argument 1: expected string, got …`).
// The answer must be ONE token for the first three and a DIFFERENT one for the fourth:
//
//   the element of an empty `[]`        no type determined      `_`
//   the key/value of an empty `Map()`   no type determined      `_`
//   an un-annotated, polymorphic param  no type determined      `_`
//   an annotation that did not resolve  the READER's type, and  `<error>`
//                                       it was rejected above
//
// The first three are one sentence to a reader — "nothing here says what this type is;
// say it" — so they are one token. Splitting them (the checker's own split is arena
// bookkeeping: an unsolved entry versus no entry at all) made the second kind look like
// a different, internal condition, which is exactly what it read as.
//
// The fourth is NOT that sentence. A reader who sees it has already been told
// `unknown type 'nosuchtype'` by name; answering `_` would send them looking for a
// missing annotation instead of at the one they wrote. `<error>`, and the angle
// brackets, are reserved for it — `soundness/hole-renders-as-blank-reject.vl` pins the
// pair from the hole's side, this file from the absence side.
//
// THE FOURTH LEG CANNOT USE THE SAME TEMPLATE, and that asymmetry is measured, not a
// gap in this file: an errored type is assignable to and from everything, so every
// assignability-shaped check ABSORBS it and reports only `unknown type '…'`. Its one
// reachable template is the `print` codegen gate below, which is not an assignability
// check. That gate is NOT a cascade of the first error either — `print` of a function
// VALUE is rejected identically when the return annotation resolves
// (`closures/print-closure-rejected.vl`), so only the RENDER comes from the error.
// @error argument 1: expected string, got _[]
// @error argument 1: expected string, got {[_]: _}
// @error argument 1: expected string, got (_) => _
// @error unknown type 'nosuchtype'
// @error print of () => <error> is type-valid but not yet supported by codegen
function ps(s: string) { print(s) }

// (1) An EMPTY ARRAY: nothing ever constrained the element type.
ps([])

// (2) An EMPTY MAP: nothing ever constrained the key type or the value type.
ps(Map())

// (3) An UN-ANNOTATED PARAMETER whose body constrains nothing — the hole. Same
// sentence, same token, and held here against (1) and (2) rather than alone. The
// FUNCTION VALUE is what is passed, deliberately: `ps(idy(1))` resolves the hole from
// the call site and renders `i32`, which would pin nothing.
function idy(x) x
ps(idy)

// (4) An ANNOTATION THAT DID NOT RESOLVE. The reader named a type; the checker
// rejected the name. Not a blank.
function mk(): nosuchtype { return 0 }
print(mk)
